  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper experimentally evaluates quantum kernel methods on a trapped‑ion quantum computer. Using the IonQ Harmony device (4 qubits), QSVC achieved test accuracies of 70% (credit card) and 100% (MNIST and Fashion‑MNIST), comparable to classical SVMs, while QSVR on financial and superconductivity datasets achieved R² values of 0.868 and 0.628 respectively, below classical SVR baselines (0.930 and 0.728). A supplementary experiment on the IonQ Aria (8 qubits) also achieved 100% accuracy on a small Fashion‑MNIST task.",
